    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d83">

                <pb facs="0092" n="82" sameAs="frus:frus1942China/pg82"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">761.94/1411</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 475</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-06-19">June 19,
                        1942</date>.<lb/>[Received July 23.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit a copy of a
                    memorandum of a conversation between a member of this Embassy and Mr. C. C.
                    Chien, Vice Chairman of the National Resources Commission, regarding Mr. Chien’s
                    views on the desirability from China’s standpoint of Russo-Japanese
                    hostilities.</p>
                <pb facs="0093" n="83" xml:id="pg83"/>
                <p>Although as far as is known Mr. Chien was not voicing the Government’s attitude,
                    it is believed that his views are shared by the majority of Chinese
                    officials.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>C. E. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d83-a1.xml" xpointer="d83-a1"/>
            </div>
